Here is a self-contained HTML file that recreates the classic 1978 Taito arcade experience of Space Invaders, with inline CSS and JS.
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>SPACE INVADERS · 1978</title>
    <style>
        * {
            box-sizing: border-box;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
        }
        body {
            background: #0a0a0a;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            min-height: 100vh;
            font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 16px;
        }
        .cabinet {
            background: #111;
            border: 4px solid #444;
            border-radius: 20px;
            box-shadow: 0 0 30px rgba(0, 200, 0, 0.2), inset 0 0 20px #000;
            padding: 20px 20px 25px;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center;
            max-width: 780px;
            width: 100%;
        }
        .bezel {
            background: #000;
            border: 2px solid #222;
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 12px 10px 10px;
            width: 100%;
            margin-bottom: 12px;
        }
        canvas {
            display: block;
            background: #000;
            width: 100%;
            height: auto;
            aspect-ratio: 640 / 720;
            border: 2px solid #333;
            image-rendering: pixelated;
            box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px #0f0;
        }
        .controls {
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            justify-content: center;
            gap: 20px 40px;
            margin-top: 16px;
            color: #8f8;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            letter-spacing: 2px;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            background: #1a1a1a;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            border-radius: 40px;
            border: 1px solid #2a2a2a;
        }
        .controls span {
            display: flex;
            gap: 8px;
            align-items: center;
        }
        .key {
            background: #222;
            border: 1px solid #555;
            border-radius: 6px;
            padding: 2px 10px;
            color: #bfb;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
        .btn {
            background: #2a2a2a;
            border: 1px solid #6a6a6a;
            border-radius: 6px;
            padding: 2px 10px;
            color: #afa;
        }
        .score-panel {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            width: 100%;
            padding: 6px 20px;
            background: #000;
            border: 1px solid #333;
            border-radius: 6px;
            margin-bottom: 6px;
            color: #0f0;
            font-size: 1.2rem;
            font-weight: bold;
            letter-spacing: 3px;
        }
        .footer {
            color: #555;
            font-size: 0.7rem;
            margin-top: 8px;
            text-align: center;
        }
        @media (max-width: 600px) {
            .controls { font-size: 0.7rem; gap: 10px; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="cabinet">
    <div class="bezel">
        <div class="score-panel">
            <span>🛸 SCORE</span>
            <span id="scoreDisplay">0000</span>
        </div>
        <canvas id="gameCanvas" width="640" height="720"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="controls">
        <span><span class="key">←</span> / <span class="key">→</span> MOVE</span>
        <span><span class="btn">SPACE</span> / <span class="btn">Z</span> FIRE</span>
        <span><span class="key">R</span> RESTART</span>
    </div>
    <div class="footer">⏤⏤⏤⏤⏤ 1978 TAITO ARCADE ⏤⏤⏤⏤⏤</div>
</div>

<script>
    (function() {
        // ---------- ORIGINAL 1978 SPECS ----------
        // 55 invaders (11x5), 2 rows of 22 points, 2 rows of 20, 1 row of 11? Actually original:
        // 5 rows of 11 = 55. Row 1 (top) = 10? No: 11 per row, 5 rows = 55.
        // Points: row1 (top) = 10, row2=20, row3=30, row4=40, row5=50? Actually original
